摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"MoonBit-native self-evolution stdio MCP plugin for DeepSeek Harness: 14 tools for scan → monitor → propose → approve → execute with deterministic rollback. DSH-only since v3.0, path-portable install since v3.1. MIT.","id":"gh:1356896306","install_available":false,"language":"MoonBit","name":"harness-self-evolution-plugin","slug":"Across2005/harness-self-evolution-plugin","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugin-market","dsh-plugins","evolution","harness","hermes","matt-pocock","mcp","moonbit","plugin-optimization","self-improvement","subagent"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"MoonBit-native self-evolution stdio MCP plugin for DeepSeek Harness: 14 tools for scan → monitor → p"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ropose → approve → execute with deterministic rollback. DSH-only since v3.0, path-portable install s"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"e → execute with deterministic rollback. DSH-only since v3.0, path-portable install since v3.1. MIT."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Harness Self-Evolution Plugin"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"A MoonBit-native plugin that scans, monitors, proposes, and validates evolutions for the DeepSeek Ha"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"rness (DSH) plugin ecosystem. Version 3.2.3. MIT."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"This plugin targets DeepSeek Harness. Deployment hinges on how DSH launches the binary, where data i"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"s read and written, and which files (patches, manifests, panels) sit alongside the binary."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Where your data lives"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"DSH resolves its home via `$DSH_HOME` (`~/.dsh` by default; a managed launcher may point it\nelsewher"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"e). The plugin mirrors that: user-scope sub-agent definitions land under\n`<DSH home>/skills/`. Full "},{"id":"p6s3","text":"install, verification, and recovery guidance:\ndocs/deploy/deepseek-harness.md."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Since v3.0.0 the plugin is **DSH-only**: the earlier claim of MiniMax Code compatibility was a\nover-"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"declaration (DSH's own source has no such host concept) and has been removed."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"If you are **writing or debugging a DSH plugin** rather than deploying this one, read docs/dsh-plugi"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"n-integration.md: the host-half / client-half contract, the Lazy-CJS client bundle rule (one stray t"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"op-level `export` breaks every plugin in the combo), `DSH_HOME` routing, and the diagnosis order for"},{"id":"p8s4","text":" \"Failed to load plugins\"."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## What it does"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"- **Scan** installed plugins across the configured scan roots for the active host\n- **Monitor** call"},{"id":"p10s2","text":" latency, success rate, token usage, retry count, and user feedback\n- **Identify** strong signals (u"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"ser override, three consecutive failures, > 20% latency regression) and medium signals (repeated par"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"ameter misuses, loop detection, repeated preferences)\n- **Propose** benchmark-driven evolutions boun"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"d to Matt Pocock engineering principles\n- **Approve** is always a human step. `auto_approve` is `fal"},{"id":"p10s6","text":"se` by default and stays `false` — the only gate against \"code changes itself into a wall\"\n- **Execu"},{"id":"p10s7","text":"te** with state machine `pending → approved → executing → completed`; real execution stays fail-clos"},{"id":"p10s8","text":"ed until a transactional sandbox adapter exists, while failed validation returns the proposal to `pe"},{"id":"p10s9","text":"nding`\n- **Sub-agent factory** persists Markdown + YAML frontmatter definitions; scope `plugin` live"},{"id":"p10s10","text":"s under the plugin's data root, scope `user` lives under `<DSH home>/skills/` (see the deploy guide)"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Architecture in one paragraph"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"The compiled binary (`bin/harness-evolution.exe`) is a stdio MCP server exposing sixteen tools. The "},{"id":"p12s2","text":"DSH\nhome resolves in `src/store/paths.mbt::dsh_home`: `$DSH_HOME` when set, else **derived from the "},{"id":"p12s3","text":"plugin's own\ninstall path** (`<X>/profiles/<name>/node_modules/...`), else `~/.dsh`. The user-scope "},{"id":"p12s4","text":"directory is\n`<DSH home>/skills` (`HARNESS_EVOLUTION_USER_DIR` overrides it), and the default scan r"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"oots follow the same\nresolved home (`src/scanner/scanner.mbt::default_scan_roots`). Since v3.0.0 the"},{"id":"p12s6","text":" multi-host abstraction is\ngone — DSH is the only target."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"See docs/code-architecture.md for the path-resolution detail."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Build"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Build prerequisites: MoonBit `>=0.1.20260904`, MSVC or Clang on Linux/macOS. The current binary in `"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"bin/harness-evolution.exe` is Windows-native; rebuilding on the target platform produces a native bi"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"nary for that platform."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The complete workspace gate also runs panel/watcher builds and an isolated desktop coexistence smoke"},{"id":"p17s2","text":" without opening a browser:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Data and configuration"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"The plugin stores proposals, metrics, signals, cache, and execution log under `$HARNESS_EVOLUTION_HO"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ME` when set; otherwise it uses the current DSH tree at `<DSH_HOME>/.harness-evolution/v2/` (with th"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"e host-compatible `~/.dsh` fallback only when no DSH tree can be resolved). Override the env var to "},{"id":"p20s4","text":"keep dev/test data separate."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Configuration is read in this order, first file that exists wins:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"1. `$HARNESS_EVOLUTION_CONFIG` (explicit override)\n2. `<cwd>/.dsh-plugin/plugin.json` (self-manifest"},{"id":"p22s2","text":")\n3. `.dsh-plugin/plugin.json` (relative to plugin root)"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"If none exist the plugin starts with built-in defaults — missing config is not a startup failure."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"> **Breaking change (unreleased v2.7.0)**: the legacy `<cwd>/.zcode-plugin/plugin.json` fallback is "},{"id":"p24s2","text":"no longer read. A deployed instance that still carries that file must rename it to `.dsh-plugin/plug"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"in.json` — the contents need no change."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Installing into the right tree (`DSH_HOME`)"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Installing is **per DSH tree**: `dsh plugin add` writes into `$DSH_HOME/profiles/<name>`, and `$DSH_"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"HOME`\ndecides which tree boots (`~/.dsh` by default — a managed launcher may point it somewhere else"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"). Trees\nshare nothing: `bundles`, `node_modules`, sessions, and skills are all per-tree, so an inst"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"all verified in\none tree stays invisible to a host booting another."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Since v3.1 the shipped mount row is **`disabled: true` and carries no machine path** — a literal pat"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"h for\none machine points at a missing file everywhere else, so the plugin would simply never mount ("},{"id":"p27s3","text":"DSH reports\none `warning` line and keeps booting: `mcp-harness-evolution` is not in the host's\n`requ"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"iredStartupEntryIds`, so its activation failure is *optional*). The row is written **per tree at\nins"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"ntryIds`, so its activation failure is *optional*). The row is written **per tree at\ninstall time**:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"`dsh.profile.bundles` and the patch layers are read at **boot**, so the host must be **restarted** b"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"efore\nthe sixteen `mcp__harness-evolution__*` tools appear in a session. The plugin additionally der"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"ives its\nown tree from the install path, so `create_sub_agent scope=user` lands in `<DSH home>/skill"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"s/` even if\n`env.DSH_HOME` were left unset."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"> **What is actually fatal, and what is not.** `failOnStartupError: true` on the mount row does **no"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"t**\n> abort the profile boot: it only rejects that one plugin's activation, and app-boot downgrades "},{"id":"p30s3","text":"it to an\n> `optional` entry warning (see the paragraph above). The genuinely fatal case is a **patch"},{"id":"p30s4","text":" layer DSH\n> cannot parse** — `parsePatchList` throws and the profile never boots. `scripts/install-"},{"id":"p30s5","text":"dsh.ps1` writes\n> that file, so its output is pinned by a regression suite that parses it with the h"},{"id":"p30s6","text":"ost's own `js-yaml`:\n>\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
